  "limitations": [
    "Known-map / simulation-truth adapters and simulated detection/instruments; no SLAM or real visual detection.",
    "The low pebble layer changes physical geometry; the previous sparse scene remains available. Mesh detail, upstream source scripts and 8K texture sizes are retained.",
    "2D circular footprint and short simulated trajectories, not a full terrain-dynamics or multi-robot traffic planner.",
    "Remaining task failures and help tasks are retained with their real reasons; not all terrain or traffic is guaranteed reachable.",
    "Contact telemetry is sampled at control snapshots, not a continuous collision-event log.",
    "One seed, one 1800s run per depth; depth3 completed fewer exploration and measurement tasks than depth1. No claim of throughput improvement.",
    "Asynchronous result timing may change subsequent greedy decisions. Predicted ETA uses path length / (0.8*max speed) plus dwell; not a learned travel-time or battery model.",
    "Centralized soft-intention coordination is an implementation choice, not a distributed wire-protocol or verbatim reproduction of MOSAIC source.",
    "Worker budget is cooperative; individual NumPy/SciPy calls are not preemptible. Current-head safety/station checks still run in the mission thread.",
    "Depth planning does not provide multi-robot space-time reservations, collision-free task-link lines, or guaranteed deadlock avoidance."
  ],
